    "body": "## Summary\n\nADR-037: `calc()` / `min()` / `max()` / `clamp()` + var()-inside-calc resolution. **First spec-driven ADR** after the arc's pivot from \"fix Wikipedia\" to \"implement CSS spec features.\"\n\n## Partial visible delta, honestly measured\n\n| Check | Before | After |\n|---|---|---|\n| Search icon width | 2 | **20** ✓ |\n| Search icon height | 0 | **0** ✗ (unchanged) |\n\nWidth grew correctly: `parse_length(\"calc(var(--font-size-medium,1rem) + 4px)\")` now resolves to 20px. Tree confirms.\n\n**Height stayed at 0** because `layout_element` doesn't currently apply `height` from ComputedStyle to non-`<img>` boxes. That's a **pre-existing gap unrelated to calc** — calc correctly evaluates the value, layout just doesn't consume it for the height property. ADR-035's img-sizing block applies width AND height, but only for `<img>`.\n\nDeferred to ADR-040 (box model completion). Documented honestly, not expanded in scope.\n\n## What shipped\n\n### 1. `eval_math_expression()` (~280 lines in style_values.cpp)\n\n- Recursive descent, standard precedence (`* /` before `+ -`)\n- Nested parens + nested `calc()`/`min()`/`max()`/`clamp()`\n- Unary negation (`calc(-1 * 12px)`)\n- `min()` / `max()` n-ary, `clamp()` ternary\n- Units: `px`, `em`, `rem`, `%`, `pt` (vh/vw deferred)\n- **Every operand converts to px at parse time** — mixed-unit arithmetic (`2em + 8px`) works via common-unit-at-parse-time\n\n14/14 verify cases pass, covering all operators + precedence + nesting + mixed units + deferred vh.\n\n### 2. `resolve_var_whole()` extended to scan-and-splice\n\n**Before**: only whole-value `var()` resolved. `calc(var(--x) + 4px)` and `border: 1px solid var(--color)` stayed raw, silently useless.\n\n**After**: any `var()` occurrence in any value resolves, recursively (nested `calc(var(--a) + calc(var(--b) * 2))` works).\n\nThis fixes ADR-026's deferred limitation, documented in `test_stylesheet.cpp` test named \"partial-value declaration left unchanged (deferred)\" — renamed to \"(resolved, ADR-037)\".\n\n## Test count\n\n- Before: 431 cases / 1765 assertions\n- After: **456 cases / 1792 assertions** (+25 / +27)\n- Full suite all pass, zero warnings\n\nNew `tests/test_calc.cpp` (~340 lines):\n- 20 `[calc]` tests covering all operators + precedence + nesting + mixed units + min/max/clamp\n- 5 `[var][adr-037]` tests covering var-inside-calc + composite values\n\n## What this unblocks (for downstream ADRs)\n\n- **Layout**: any future feature using calc() for spacing, sizing, or offset — currently ~30 declarations on Wikipedia resolve to 0, now to their real values\n- **Typography**: `calc()` for responsive font sizes once `calc()` in font-size path is wired (separate small ADR)\n- **Composition**: `border: 1px solid var(--color)` and every other composite-with-var pattern\n- **Foundation**: same parser handles `clamp()` for responsive design (widely used in modern CSS)\n\n## What's still deferred\n\n- `height` applied to non-img boxes (ADR-040 box model)\n- `vh` / `vw` (need viewport_height in LengthContext)\n- Vertical `%` inside calc (same)\n- `calc()` in grid-track sizing / font-size (different code paths)\n- `attr()`, `counter()` (depend on pseudo-elements, ADR-039)\n\n## Verification checklist\n\n| Check | Result |\n|---|---|\n| `calc(10px + 5px)` = 15 | ✓ |\n| `calc(2em + 8px)` = 40 (mixed-unit) | ✓ |\n| `calc(100% - 20px)` = 780 | ✓ |\n| `calc(10px * 2)` = 20, `calc(100px / 4)` = 25 | ✓ |\n| `calc(10px + 5px * 2)` = 20 (precedence) | ✓ |\n| `calc((10px + 5px) * 2)` = 30 (parens) | ✓ |\n| `calc(-1 * 12px)` = -12 (unary) | ✓ |\n| `calc(calc(10px + 5px) * 2)` = 30 (nested) | ✓ |\n| `min(10,20)` / `max(10,20)` / `clamp(10,50,20)` | ✓ |\n| var() inside calc resolves | ✓ |\n| Composite `border: 1px solid var(--color)` resolves | ✓ |\n| Non-calc paths unchanged (`10px`, `2em`, `auto`) | ✓ |\n| Full suite green | ✓ |\n\nRefs #191\n",
